        <item>
            <title>0.2</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:08:26 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>173</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 173)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Voice notes replay the picture.</b> A note now remembers where the playhead went while you were talking — play it back and the shot follows. Long notes get a scrubber so you can jump to the part you want.</li>
<li><b>Comments as subtitles</b>: tick the box when exporting a movie and your notes burn in over the frames they were made about.</li>
<li><b>EXR timecode</b> is read from the file header, alongside the QuickTime timecode support added in the last build.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
